# SpecView

> Lede 0.7.0's docs for SpecView, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/json-render.md

SpecView draws a json-render spec with Lede, so a model’s reply can be a screen. `catalog` lists the components a model may use and goes into its prompt, `registry` draws each one and `check` finds the props and bindings a spec gets wrong.

Experimental: its props can change in a minor release, which the CHANGELOG names. An item is experimental for the release that adds it, and stable once a release ships it unchanged.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/json-render
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md), [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md), [`theme-provider`](theme-provider.md), [`button`](button.md), [`checkbox`](checkbox.md), [`list`](list.md), [`segmented-control`](segmented-control.md), [`switch`](switch.md), [`text-field`](text-field.md), [`empty-state`](empty-state.md), [`form-section`](form-section.md), [`page-header`](page-header.md) and [`summary-card`](summary-card.md), and the npm packages `@json-render/core@0.22.0`, `@json-render/react@0.22.0` and `zod@^4.6.7`. The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.7.0/json-render.json.

