## Props

The screen a spec describes, drawn with Lede. It draws once the spec's root element arrives, and state that arrives after it, as a model streams it, fills in what's drawn: a list drawn with repeat gains a row per item. The person can use the screen while the rest streams in.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `spec` (required) | `Spec \| null` |  | The spec so far, such as `specFromParts(message.parts)` while a reply streams. |
| `streaming` | `boolean` |  | True while the spec streams: elements still on their way draw nothing until they arrive. |
| `headingLevel` | `2 \| 3` | `2` | The level of the spec's title. Default 2, under a page's h1; a chat message's author heading makes it 3. |
| `handlers` | `SpecHandlers` |  | Called when the spec runs a catalog action. Read through a ref, so each call reaches the latest, and an inline object is fine. One that returns a promise holds the actions after it until it settles. An action whose params read a field that fails its check doesn't run, so its handler isn't called. |
| `fallback` | `ComponentRenderer` |  | Drawn for an element whose type the registry doesn't have, such as one from a newer catalog. Without it, that element draws nothing and json-render logs a warning. |
| `onStateChange` | `(state: State) => void` |  | Called with the screen's whole state after each change, such as for a chat to send what the person entered. |
| `onActionHeld` | `(held: HeldAction) => void` |  | Called when an action doesn't run because fields it reads fail their checks, with the action and each field's name and the error it shows. Read through a ref, so an inline function is fine. |

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import type { Spec } from '@json-render/core';
import { SpecView } from '@/components/lede/json-render/spec-view';

// A spec, such as a model's reply, drawn with Lede. Its switches are bound to the spec's own state.
const spec: Spec = {
  root: 'screen',
  state: { alerts: { push: true } },
  elements: {
    screen: { type: 'Screen', props: {}, children: ['header', 'delivery'] },
    header: { type: 'PageHeader', props: { title: 'Notifications', summary: 'Choose where alerts reach you.' }, children: [] },
    delivery: { type: 'ListGroup', props: { title: 'Delivery' }, children: ['push'] },
    push: { type: 'ListRow', props: { title: 'Push alerts', checked: { $bindState: '/alerts/push' } }, children: [] },
  },
};

export function Notifications() {
  return <SpecView spec={spec} />;
}
```

